PANGU — Parthenon-based Astrophysics: Numerical Relativity and GRMHD, Unified

PANGU is a clean Parthenon application architecture informed by the public AthenaK,
AthenaPK, KHARMA, and Parthenon code bases. PANGU source files carry their own license;
the bundled or sibling upstream projects retain their original licenses and notices.

The PPMC reconstruction in src/reconstruct/hydro_reconstruction.h is a PANGU-adapted
derivative of AthenaPK src/recon/ppm_simple.hpp. Its applicable upstream notices are:
Copyright (c) 2020-2021, Athena-Parthenon Collaboration; Copyright (c) 2020,
James M. Stone and the Athena code team. It is distributed under BSD-3-Clause.

The Newtonian MHD LLF/HLLE/HLLD algebra and Gardiner--Stone corner-EMF formulas in
src/mhd are PANGU adaptations of the corresponding AthenaK algorithms. AthenaK is
Copyright (c) 2020 James M. Stone and the AthenaK team and is distributed under
BSD-3-Clause. PANGU replaces AthenaK mesh, communication, and task infrastructure with
Parthenon Face/Edge metadata, communication, AMR, and task APIs.

The stage-1 advection smoke problem follows the public Parthenon advection example's
driver/task concepts and APIs, but is organized behind PANGU-owned registries, package
boundaries, parameter schema, provenance, test harness, and input layout. See
docs/migration/license_inventory.md and docs/migration/source_disposition.md.
